      "method": "Per wet group (24 phases 0, 2, ... 46; each rendered as its own item; the five-pod run claimed items in chunks of four,\nchunk = (global item - 1) // 4, read from frames.json):\n  1. two-level patterns over the 24 phases inside the group's alpha; a pattern constant inside every worker chunk is a\n     worker switch (removed), the others are real (kept, guarded);\n  2. per switch, largest first, near its own pixels: step c = mean(on) - mean(off); where clear (|luma c| >= 0.75,\n     t >= 5) the pixel is set to the target state (draft 32's state where it is clear, else the time average);\n  3. pixels flat inside every chunk but stepping between chunks take their median over the 24 phases;\n  4. then exactly pack95's method: occluder picture = per-channel minimum of the phases (live alpha; for the groups\n     whose shape changed in Brief 95, RGB zeroed where a phase's alpha is 0, as pack95 did), slices cut by the live\n     slice alphas (must rebuild the parent), wet sheets = phase - parent inside each slice's mask (48 frames, phase\n     f // 2 * 2, 8 x 6 sheet), all wet sheets the manifest lists are kept. Full stills and ad overlays rebuilt by\n     pack95's own production.full_stills_ads."
